PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Round-0 belief in A remains intact and strengthened. Core preserved algebra (unchanged across rounds): all-or-nothing fixes fraction p fully protected; cases_v=(1-p)·cases_u exactly, but PT_v>(1-p)·PT_u because protected never exit risk set under irreversible infection + exchangeable exposure. Thus time-averaged IRR<1-p so 1-IRR>p (overestimate). Bias absent for leaky model and for cumulative-incidence ratios; grows with follow-up length or depletion. 

Round-1 public split: A side (Colleagues 1,3,4,6,7,10-12,15-18) supplies consistent derivations of differential PT inflation and notes that C arguments equate observed IR to instantaneous hazard among susceptibles only (or assume fixed PT). C side (Colleagues 2,5,8,9,13,14) insists standard IR definition already incorporates all randomized PT so ratio stays identically 1-p under constant λ; claims A side conflates IR with cumulative incidence. No numerical counter-example or explicit integral supplied by either side. B claims remain minority and sign-reversed.

Unresolved tension: whether epidemiological IR (events/total observed PT until event/censoring) is the time-integrated quantity or the constant instantaneous rate. Belief update: none—A is correct once PT definition is used; C responses continue to replace observed rate with hazard among susceptibles. Model-independent result for closed cohort preserved for later rounds.}

